//FLESH-TEARER +2 - 4500mo//
COPY "rick_bigg_mod/items/TB#BLUN.itm" "override"
	SAY NAME1 "Flail"
	SAY UNIDENTIFIED_DESC "The flail is a sturdy wooden handle attached to an iron rod, a wooden rod with spikes, or a spiked iron ball. Between the handle and its implement is either a hinge or chain link. The weapon was originally used as a tool for threshing grain.

STATISTICS:

Damage: 1d10 (crushing or piercing)
Speed Factor: 7
Proficiency Type: Flail/Morning Star
Type: One-handed
Requires:
 15 Strength

Weight: 15"

	SAY NAME2 "Flesh-Tearer +2"
	SAY DESC "This brutal weapon was forged by a mad duergar smith who sought to combine the bone-shattering impact of a flail with the horrific lacerations of a broadsword. The spiked iron heads feature jagged, razor-sharp ridges that spin violently when swung. The result is a terrifying weapon that not only crushes the armor of its victims but also shears through leather and flesh with a grotesque tearing sound.o commemorate the defeat of the devil Belhifet. It was meant to always remain within the town of Easthaven to remind the people of the great evil that had been barely defeated. 

STATISTICS:

THAC0: +2
Damage: 1d10+2, +3 slashing damage
Damage type: (crushing or piercing)
Speed Factor: 4
Proficiency Type: Flail/Morning Star
Type: One-handed
Requires:
 15 Strength

Weight: 9"




//DEFENDER OF EASTHEAVEN +4 - 14000mo//
COPY "rick_bigg_mod/items/WAFLAIL.itm" "override"
	SAY NAME1 "Flail"
	SAY UNIDENTIFIED_DESC "The flail is a sturdy wooden handle attached to an iron rod, a wooden rod with spikes, or a spiked iron ball. Between the handle and its implement is either a hinge or chain link. The weapon was originally used as a tool for threshing grain.

STATISTICS:

Damage: 1d10 (crushing or piercing)
Speed Factor: 7
Proficiency Type: Flail/Morning Star
Type: One-handed
Requires:
 15 Strength

Weight: 15"

	SAY NAME2 "Defender of Eastheaven +3"
	SAY DESC "This flail was created a century ago to commemorate the defeat of the devil Belhifet. It was meant to always remain within the town of Easthaven to remind the people of the great evil that had been barely defeated. 

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:

– +10% resistance to slashing, piercing, and crushing damage

THAC0: +4
Damage: 1d10+4 (crushing or piercing)
Speed Factor: 4
Proficiency Type: Flail/Morning Star
Type: One-handed
Requires:
 15 Strength

Weight: 9"









//FLAIL OF AGES +3 - 12000mo//
COPY "rick_bigg_mod/items/BLUN14.itm" "override"
	SAY NAME1 "Flail"
	SAY UNIDENTIFIED_DESC "The flail is a sturdy wooden handle attached to an iron rod, a wooden rod with spikes, or a spiked iron ball. Between the handle and its implement is either a hinge or chain link. The weapon was originally used as a tool for threshing grain.

STATISTICS:

Damage: 1d10 (crushing or piercing)
Speed Factor: 7
Proficiency Type: Flail/Morning Star
Type: One-handed
Requires:
 15 Strength

Weight: 15"

	SAY NAME2 "Flail of Ages +3"
	SAY DESC "This flail has been in the care of Lord de'Arnise for some time, a relic of his adventuring youth. It has been kept disassembled, the individual pieces stored in separate locations, and only used in the direst of emergencies. Lord de'Arnise was likely concerned about the powerful magic that the weapon radiated when compiled, and rightfully so. A trail of destruction has followed it through history, leading straight back to the original owners. The flail was the creation of the warlike rakshasa, a race of vengeful spirits that crave human meat, and used as an adaptable weapon that could suit any battle. During a particularly violent hunt, the flail was lost, only to be returned when they used their affinity for magic to locate its powerful aura. They discovered that the weapon had found its way into the hands of a great human warrior, and the battle that followed was truly splendid. They have since used the item as bait countless times, 'losing' it again and again. Powerful items gravitate toward powerful people, and powerful people yield the most glorious battles.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
- Armor Class: +1 vs. Slashing, Piercing and Crushing

Combat abilities:
– 30% chance of slowing target for 3 rounds

THAC0: +3
Damage: 1d10+3, +1 acid damage, +1 cold damage, +1 fire damage
Damage type: Crushing or Piercing
Speed Factor: 4
Proficiency Type: Flail/Morning Star
Type: One-handed
Requires:
 15 Strength

Weight: 10"




//FLAIL OF AGES +4 - 15000mo//
COPY "rick_bigg_mod/items/BLUN30C.itm" "override"
	SAY NAME1 "Flail"
	SAY UNIDENTIFIED_DESC "The flail is a sturdy wooden handle attached to an iron rod, a wooden rod with spikes, or a spiked iron ball. Between the handle and its implement is either a hinge or chain link. The weapon was originally used as a tool for threshing grain.

STATISTICS:

Damage: 1d10 (crushing or piercing)
Speed Factor: 7
Proficiency Type: Flail/Morning Star
Type: One-handed
Requires:
 15 Strength

Weight: 15"

	SAY NAME2 "Flail of Ages +4"
	SAY DESC "This flail has been in the care of Lord de'Arnise for some time, a relic of his adventuring youth. It has been kept disassembled, the individual pieces stored in separate locations, and only used in the direst of emergencies. Lord de'Arnise was likely concerned about the powerful magic that the weapon radiated when compiled, and rightfully so. A trail of destruction has followed it through history, leading straight back to the original owners. The flail was the creation of the warlike rakshasa, a race of vengeful spirits that crave human meat, and used as an adaptable weapon that could suit any battle. During a particularly violent hunt, the flail was lost, only to be returned when they used their affinity for magic to locate its powerful aura. They discovered that the weapon had found its way into the hands of a great human warrior, and the battle that followed was truly splendid. They have since used the item as bait countless times, 'losing' it again and again. Powerful items gravitate toward powerful people, and powerful people yield the most glorious battles.
	
	This four-headed flail causes fire, cold, acid, and poison damage. If the fifth head for the Flail of Ages could be found, it would make this awesome weapon even more powerful.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
- Armor Class: +1 vs. Slashing, Piercing and Crushing

Combat abilities:
– 30% chance each hit that target will be slowed for 3 rounds

THAC0: +4
Damage: 1d10+4, +1 fire damage, +1 cold damage, +1 acid damage, +1 poison damage
Damage type: Crushing or Piercing
Speed Factor: 3
Proficiency Type: Flail/Morning Star
Type: One-handed
Requires:
 15 Strength

Weight: 9"






